                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 16 at 6:40AM MDT until September 16 at 9:30AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "At 640 AM MDT, emergency management reported flash flooding in\nRuidoso area, including areas downstream of the Salt burn scar. Up to\n2 inches of rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 2 inches\nin 1 hour. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in\nthe warned area. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing flash\nflooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported flash flooding in the Ruidoso\narea, including along Cree Meadows Drive, White Mountain\nDrive, and along Cedar Creek and Fence Canyon.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nRuidoso, Ruidoso Downs and Hollywood.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
